\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterbeamshape}{{1.8}{36}{Top panel: the radius of the beam as it travels from the SRM (z = 0) to the waist of the OMC. Significant points along the axis are marked with vertical lines. Less significant, but useful reference points, are marked by dashed vertical lines. Bottom panel: The gouy phase shift accumulated by the beam as it propagates along the optical axis.\relax }{figure.caption.63}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.9}{\ignorespaces Top panel: The choice of OFI lens power effects the combination of OMx1 and OMX2 power required for 100\% mode matching. Bottom panel: The best choice of OFI lens corresponds to where the Gouy phase separation between the pair of OMx1 and OMx2 mirrors that give 100\% mode matching is closest to 45\si {\degree }. The optimal Gouy phase separation between OMx1 and OMX2 achievable by this layout is 43\si {\degree }.\relax }}{37}{figure.caption.64}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterlenschoice}{{1.9}{37}{Top panel: The choice of OFI lens power effects the combination of OMx1 and OMX2 power required for 100\% mode matching. Bottom panel: The best choice of OFI lens corresponds to where the Gouy phase separation between the pair of OMx1 and OMx2 mirrors that give 100\% mode matching is closest to 45\si {\degree }. The optimal Gouy phase separation between OMx1 and OMX2 achievable by this layout is 43\si {\degree }.\relax }{figure.caption.64}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.10}{\ignorespaces Astigmatism is a source of loss. When designing this layout, to explore how sensitive it was to astigmatism, the AOI for the curved mirrors was altered. Using equation \ref  {eq:bhd_for_ligo_mm_loss}, the loss was computed. This effect is negligible up to 10\si {\degree }, after which it starts to become significant compared to the losses summarised in table \ref  {tab:HAM6_losses}.\relax }}{38}{figure.caption.65}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterastigmatism}{{1.10}{38}{Astigmatism is a source of loss. When designing this layout, to explore how sensitive it was to astigmatism, the AOI for the curved mirrors was altered. Using equation \ref {eq:bhd_for_ligo_mm_loss}, the loss was computed. This effect is negligible up to 10\si {\degree }, after which it starts to become significant compared to the losses summarised in table \ref {tab:HAM6_losses}.\relax }{figure.caption.65}{}}
